Expected values: what FireEye's BitsParser reads from the fixtures with
carving on (--carvedb), one TSV per fixture. gen.sh writes them; see its
header for the versions run, and bitsparser_tsv.py for the columns.

BitsParser prints each distinct record once (live jobs, carved jobs, and,
for qmgr.db, file records it couldn't tie to a job). tests/oracle.rs finds
each of them among this crate's jobs and files, field by field (the fields
BitsParser leaves empty are not compared), and counts what this crate reads
beyond them.
